---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: What the demo starts
    accDescr: docker compose up first runs the container secrets, which makes the password into demo/.env and a volume. Paperless-ngx with Redis and Nextcloud with PostgreSQL, the cron and a worker then start from that volume, and the app comes from the App Store or the checkout. The container init fills Paperless with the synthetic documents, creates the user demo and the account of the app, connects the app, starts a dry run and then the first run, and prints where everything is.

    up["docker compose up"]
    secrets["secrets:<br>one password, in<br>demo/.env and a volume"]
    paperless["Paperless-ngx<br>with Redis,<br>on 127.0.0.1:8581"]
    nextcloud["Nextcloud with<br>PostgreSQL, cron and<br>a worker, on 127.0.0.1:8580"]
    app["The app from the<br>App Store, or the checkout<br>with compose.local.yaml"]
    init["init: 15 synthetic documents,<br>the user demo, the account of the app,<br>a dry run, the first run"]
    ready["The archive in Files,<br>with 14 documents"]

    up --> secrets
    secrets --> paperless
    secrets --> nextcloud
    app --> nextcloud
    paperless --> init
    nextcloud --> init
    init --> ready

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class up person
    class secrets,paperless,nextcloud,app,init bot
    class ready done
